<ArticleLayout slug="douyin-ad-creative-specs-by-format" ctaLabel="Talk to the production team" faq={faq}>
  <p class="standfirst">The pages ranking for Douyin ad specs are media-buying articles about ad types and costs. The few that print dimensions are reprinting a spec sheet from the end of 2020, and sometimes attaching it to the wrong format.</p>

  <h2>What are the Douyin TopView creative specs?</h2>

  <p>A video of 10 to 60 seconds, most commonly published, whose first 3 seconds play full screen before it settles into the feed. That timing is well agreed. The file specs are not published for TopView on any Douyin source at all, and the sizes you may have been sent under that name belong to a different format.</p>

  <h2>How to read these numbers</h2>

  <p>These specs are not read from an advertiser backend. Ocean Engine, the platform that sells Douyin ads, returns no specification text to anyone not logged in, so no open source reaches the official value.</p>

  <p>What follows is the most commonly published figure for each spec, collected across 17 independent sources in Chinese and English on 10 September 2026, with the number of sources that agreed shown per row. Rows marked consensus had broad agreement. Rows marked contested did not, and those carry the full spread rather than a single number.</p>

  <p>Treat this as the best available public reading, not as the rule. Platform specs change without announcement and often without an English notice at all. Before you build a batch to any number on this page, open your own advertiser account and confirm it there. Reviewed 10 September 2026.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Ocean Engine does not publish its ad creative specs where a brand can read them. On 10 September 2026 its developer documentation returned a page title and no text, and its help center returned an empty page. The most detailed Douyin spec sheet anyone can open without an account is a rate card for the fourth quarter of 2020, valid for three months, which says its own online version takes precedence. Every figure below is the most commonly published value, not a value read from the platform.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: four Ocean Engine surfaces fetched unauthenticated on 10 September 2026, plus 17 published sources carrying a Douyin paid-ad spec, 16 Chinese-language and 1 English-language, counted per value. Modal values, not primary readings.</p>

  <p>A three-month rate card that defers to an online version nobody outside can read. That is the ground every Douyin ad spec in public circulation stands on.</p>

  <h2>What are the open screen ad requirements?</h2>

  <p>Open screen is the ad that plays as the app opens, and it has the most settled row on this page.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Open screen timing is the one Douyin ad spec the sources agree on. A static image shows for 3 seconds, an animated image for 4, a video for 5. All five Chinese-language sources that give display times give the same three, on pages dated from 2018 to 2025.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: 5 published sources, Chinese-language, collected 10 September 2026, counted per value with no contradicting source. Modal value, not a primary reading.</p>

  <p>Everything else about open screen comes from spec sheets with a date on them, and the date matters.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">The newest complete Douyin open screen spec sheet in public circulation dates from the fourth quarter of 2020. Between the 2018 and 2020 versions the static image cap rose from under 150KB to under 300KB and the largest canvas grew to 1080 by 2340. Nothing publicly reachable shows what changed after that.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: two rate card generations, 2018 and 2020, both Chinese-language, read 10 September 2026. An observation about age, not a current value.</p>

