  <p>Export under 100MB at 720 by 1280 or above and you clear every file and resolution figure in circulation. Duration is the row to confirm in the account, since the single 2024 page and the four older ones point in different directions.</p>

  <h2>Search ads</h2>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Douyin search ads publish no creative spec of their own on any source found. On Douyin they run as video, with one ad mixed into results positions 2 to 10 and the first position held for an exact brand-name search.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: 2 published sources, Chinese-language, collected 10 September 2026. Modal value, not a primary reading, and an absence stated with its search date.</p>

  <p>No separate spec means the in-feed video figures are the only published guide, which is a reasonable working assumption to confirm rather than a rule.</p>

  <h2>Why was my Douyin ad creative rejected?</h2>

  <p>No rejection notice was obtained for this page, and no source ranks why Douyin ad creative gets rejected, so there is no list of top reasons to give. What has been reported is how rejections now arrive.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Rejection notices have become more specific. Since an AI review upgrade reported for October 2025, a rejected video is flagged at the second, or the line of dialogue, where the problem sits, rather than rejected as a whole.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: 2 published sources, Chinese-language, one dated 2026, collected 10 September 2026. Modal value, not a primary reading.</p>

  <p>That changes the fix more than the cause. A flag at a timestamp means a recut of a few seconds rather than a new edit, which is worth building into the schedule: keep the project file open and the source footage to hand until review clears.</p>

  <h2>Where this leaves a brief</h2>

  <p>Three rows are solid enough to build to: open screen display times, the TopView 3-second opening and hand-off, and the in-feed 9:16 frame at 720 by 1280 or above. Everything else is either dated, contested, or not published, and this page labels which.</p>

  <p>The <a href="/solutions/platforms/douyin">Douyin platform page</a> covers producing for Douyin as a whole, the <a href="/services/design/ad-creative">ad creative design service page</a> covers building the formats themselves, and the <a href="/resources/insights/douyin-video-specs-safe-zones">article on Douyin video specs and safe zones</a> covers the organic post frame and the safe box that clears both Douyin and TikTok figures.</p>

  <p>Reviewed 10 September 2026. Confirm every figure in your own advertiser account before building a batch to it.</p>

  <h2>Questions about Douyin ad specs</h2>

  <h3>What are the Douyin TopView creative specs?</h3>

  <p>The most commonly published TopView duration is 10 to 60 seconds, on four of five Douyin sources, with the first 3 seconds full screen and the ad becoming a feed post from the fourth second. No Douyin source publishes a TopView resolution, file size, format or bitrate, and the sizes often circulated under that name are a 2020 open screen file set.</p>

  <h3>What size is a Douyin in-feed ad?</h3>

  <p>A 9:16 vertical video, with 16:9 also accepted. Pages dated 2023 and 2024 put the floor at 720 by 1280, while older pages say 540 by 960. File caps are unsettled at 100MB to 1,000MB, so a file under 100MB clears every published figure. Confirm in your advertiser account before exporting a batch.</p>

  <h3>What are the open screen ad requirements?</h3>

  <p>Display times are agreed on all five sources giving them: 3 seconds for a static image, 4 for an animated image, 5 for video. The most detailed public sheet dates from late 2020, giving a 5-second silent MP4 at 5MB or under and a static image cap under 300KB. Treat those figures as dated rather than current.</p>

  <h3>Why was my Douyin ad creative rejected?</h3>

  <p>No source ranks rejection reasons, so there is no published top list. What has been reported is the format of the notice: since an AI review upgrade reported for October 2025, a rejected video is flagged at the second or line of dialogue where the problem sits, which usually means a short recut rather than a new edit.</p>

  <h3>How long can a Douyin ad video be?</h3>

  <p>It depends on the format. TopView is most commonly published at 10 to 60 seconds. In-feed video appears as 5 to 60 seconds on four pages dated to 2023 and 4 to 300 seconds on the only 2024 page. Open screen video runs 5 seconds. Confirm the current limits in your advertiser account.</p>
